#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:1
msgid "Runtime settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:3
msgid "Selecting between multiple object factories"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:5
msgid ""
"The `vtkObjectFactory` mechanism supports registering multiple "
"implementations of a class at runtime. By default, VTK uses the first "
"registered implementation, which can cause conflicts if different modules "
"register different implementations of the same class."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:7
msgid ""
"To control which implementation is selected, provide a preferences string to "
"`vtkObjectFactory`. The string lists attribute keys with a list of values "
"using the format `key=value1,value2`, and separates attributes with "
"semicolons (e.g., `keyA=valueA1,valueA2;keyB=valueB1,valueB2`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:9
msgid "There are three possible ways to set the preferences are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:10
msgid ""
"Set the environment variable `VTK_FACTORY_PREFER` before starting your "
"application."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:11
msgid "VTK_FACTORY_PREFER=\"keyA=valueA1,valueA2;keyB=valueB1,valueB2\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:14
msgid ""
"Call the static method `vtkObjectFactory::SetPreferences()` before creating "
"any VTK objects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:16
msgid ""
"vtkObjectFactory::SetPreferences(\"keyA=valueA1,valueA2;keyB=valueB1,"
"valueB2\");\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:19
msgid ""
"Call the static method `vtkObjectFactory::"
"InitializePreferencesFromCommandLineArgs(argc, argv)` early in your "
"application, passing the command line arguments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:21
msgid ""
"int main(int argc, char* argv[])\n"
"{\n"
"  vtkObjectFactory::InitializePreferencesFromCommandLineArgs(argc, argv);\n"
"  // ...\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:29
msgid ""
"# Example preference string ('=' sign can be omitted and replaced with a "
"space)\n"
"./my_vtk_app --vtk-factory-prefer=\"keyA=valueA1,valueA2;keyB=valueB1,"
"valueB2\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:34
msgid ""
"When preferences are passed to the object factory, the choice of the class "
"to instantiate is based on a score. The factory will assign a score to all "
"classes that derive from the given class name to instantiate. The class with "
"the highest score will be chosen one. The score calculation is explained in "
"the section below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:36
msgid "Override Attributes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:38
msgid ""
"Here is a list of attributes that are recognized in the VTK factory "
"preferences string. These attributes are used as keys in the "
"`VTK_FACTORY_PREFER` environment variable (or equivalently via "
"`vtkObjectFactory::SetPreferences()` or the `--vtk-factory-prefer` command-"
"line option) using the format described above (for example: `Platform=macOS;"
"RenderingBackend=OpenGL`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:0
msgid "Attribute Name"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:0
msgid "Possible Values"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:0
msgid "Platform"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:0
msgid "`Embedded`,`iOS`,`macOS`,`WebAssembly`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:0
msgid "RenderingBackend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:0
msgid "`OpenGL`, `WebGPU`, `ANARI`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:0
msgid "WindowSystem"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:0
msgid "`Cocoa`,`EGL`,`HTML5`,`OffScreenMESA`,`X11`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:0
msgid "SupportRenderPass"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:0
msgid "`true`, `false`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:47
msgid ""
"The class score is computed based on the override attributes above by "
"comparing them against the preference keys and values. Three rules influence "
"the score value:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:48
msgid ""
"If the attribute key is not found in the preferences, the score stays the "
"same."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:49
msgid ""
"If the attribute key is found and the preference value matches, the score is "
"incremented by 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:50
msgid ""
"If the attribute key is found and the preference value does not match, the "
"score is decremented by 1. Once all class scores are computed, the class "
"with the highest score is chosen. If multiple classes have the same highest "
"score value, the order of the preferences value determines which class to "
"pick. Finally, if all scores have a value of 0, the factory will fallback to "
"the default instantiation mechanism."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:53
msgid ""
"As an example, if `ANARI` and `OpenGL` are activated on a build, here are "
"some possible score results for a `vtkRenderWindow` instantiation:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:54
msgid ""
"`VTK_FACTORY_PREFER=\"RenderingBackend=OpenGL,ANARI;SupportRenderPass=true\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:55
msgid ""
"`vtkOpenGLRenderWindow` will have a score of 2 because it matches both keys "
"and values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:56
msgid ""
"`vtkAnariRenderWindow` will have a score of 1 because it only matches the "
"`RenderingBackend` key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:57
msgid ""
"`VTK_FACTORY_PREFER=\"RenderingBackend=OpenGL,ANARI;"
"SupportRenderPass=false\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:58
msgid ""
"`vtkOpenGLRenderWindow` will have a score of 1 because it only matches the "
"`RenderingBackend` key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:59
msgid ""
"`vtkAnariRenderWindow` will have a score of 2 because it only matches both "
"keys and values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:60
msgid "`VTK_FACTORY_PREFER=\"RenderingBackend=ANARI;SupportRenderPass=true\"`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:61
msgid ""
"The score will be 0 for both render windows because `vtkAnariRenderWindow` "
"matches the first key and `vtkOpenGLRenderWindow` matches the second key. In "
"this case, the factory will fallback to default factory instantiation "
"mechanism."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:63
msgid "OpenGL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:65
msgid ""
"On Linux and Windows, VTK will attempt to detect support for an OpenGL "
"context backend at runtime and create an appropriate subclass of "
"`vtkOpenGLRenderWindow`. You can override this process by specifying an "
"environment variable `VTK_DEFAULT_OPENGL_WINDOW`. The possible values are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:70
msgid ""
"`vtkXOpenGLRenderWindow` (Linux; applicable only when `VTK_USE_X` is `ON`, "
"which is the default setting)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:71
msgid ""
"`vtkWin32OpenGLRenderWindow` (Windows; applicable only when "
"`VTK_USE_WIN32_OPENGL` is `ON`, which is the default setting)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:72
msgid ""
"`vtkEGLRenderWindow` (applicable only when `VTK_OPENGL_HAS_EGL` is `ON`, "
"which is the default setting)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:73
msgid ""
"`vtkOSOpenGLRenderWindow` (OSMesa, requires that `osmesa.dll` or `libOSMesa."
"so` is installed)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:75
msgid ""
"Note: VTK does **not** support OSMesa on macOS, iOS, Android and WebAssembly "
"platforms."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:77
msgid "Multisample anti-aliasing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:79
msgid ""
"Some OpenGL drivers have rendering problems when Multisample anti-aliasing "
"is enabled. It is possible to specify the environment variable "
"`VTK_FORCE_MSAA` to troubleshoot rendering problems with these values:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:82
msgid "`0` to disable MSAA"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/runtime_settings.md:83
msgid ""
"`1` to enable it regardless even when the driver is known to have problems "
"with MSAA"
msgstr ""
